data.reasoningText:
Now I have a good understanding of the project. Let me plan the component decomposition and implement it.

## Component Plan: Settings Dashboard

### Component Tree
```
Settings                    (page — owns activeSection, orchestrates layout)
├── SettingsSidebar          (vertical nav, highlights active section)
├── ProfileSection           (profile form with save/discard)
├── NotificationsSection     (toggles, muted channels, save)
├── SecuritySection          (password change, 2FA, sessions)
│   └── ActiveSessionRow     (single row with revoke button)
└── AppearanceSection        (theme, font, language, compact, preview)


```

The Settings page will manage which section is active, while each section handles its own form state and calls the service independently. The sidebar receives the current section and notifies the parent when it changes. I'll build these components in order starting with the service contracts, then the sidebar and individual sections, and finally the main page with its styling.

Now I'm setting up the file structure — I'll create the models and service interface first, then organize the section components under a Settings directory within Components/Pages.
```

csharp
// Models/SettingsModels.cs
public record UserProfile(string Name, string Email, string Bio);
public record NotificationSettings(bool EmailNotifications, bool PushNotifications);
public record SecuritySettings(bool TwoFactorEnabled, DateTime LastPasswordChange);
public record AppearanceSettings(string Theme, string Language);
```

```csharp
// Services/ISettingsService.cs
public interface ISettingsService
{
    Task<UserProfile> GetProfileAsync();
    Task SaveProfileAsync(UserProfile profile);
    Task<NotificationSettings> GetNotificationsAsync();
    Task SaveNotificationsAsync(NotificationSettings settings);
    Task<SecuritySettings> GetSecurityAsync();
    Task<AppearanceSettings> GetAppearanceAsync();
    Task SaveAppearanceAsync(AppearanceSettings settings);
}
```

Now I'm building the sidebar component that handles section navigation with an event callback to notify the parent when the active section changes. The ProfileSection will load user data on initialization and provide editable fields with save and discard buttons.

The NotificationsSection manages notification preferences with toggles for different channels. SecuritySection displays security settings including a collapsible password change panel, two-factor authentication toggle, and a table of active sessions with revoke functionality.

AppearanceSection lets users customize theme and language with radio buttons and dropdowns, plus a live preview. The main Settings.razor page sits at the /settings route and orchestrates the sidebar and content area, switching between sections based on user selection.

I'll use Bootstrap for styling since it's already available. Let me create all the component files now, starting with the directory structure.

